WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.886 --> 00:00:14.590
"I was forced to leave home ten years ago."

2
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:17.851
Miles began his story while Edward continued to eat.

3
00:00:19.532 --> 00:00:21.353
Edward raised his eyebrows in surprise.

4
00:00:21.373 --> 00:00:29.620
"Why?" "I'm from a wealthy noble family," Miles said.

5
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.002
"My mother died when I was young.

6
00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:34.465
My father, Sir Richard, is a kind man.

7
00:00:35.766 --> 00:00:37.248
So is my older brother, Arthur.

8
00:00:38.369 --> 00:00:42.213
But my younger brother, Hugh, is evil and plotted against me.

9
00:00:42.853 --> 00:00:47.938
We—" "I don't have any brothers, just one sister," Edward interrupted.

10
00:00:47.958 --> 00:00:51.001
"Yes, Your Majesty."

11
00:00:52.122 --> 00:00:53.484
Miles continued the story.

12
00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:59.448
"We have a dear friend, Lady Edith, whose family is even wealthier than mine.

13
00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.332
Her parents are dead, and she has no siblings.

14
00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.275
So my father is her guardian.

15
00:01:08.876 --> 00:01:10.998
Beautiful, wonderful Edith!"

16
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.161
Miles paused and sighed.

17
00:01:14.181 --> 00:01:21.307
"I always loved her even though she was engaged to Arthur from an early age.

18
00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:25.005
And I know that she loved me."

19
00:01:28.207 --> 00:01:29.828
Edward pointed his fork at Miles.

20
00:01:29.848 --> 00:01:33.951
"You're not supposed to be in love with your brother's fiancée.

21
00:01:35.212 --> 00:01:36.352
Even I know that."

22
00:01:36.372 --> 00:01:39.314
"Oh, but Arthur didn't care.

23
00:01:40.895 --> 00:01:43.877
He was in love with someone else and wanted to break the engagement.

24
00:01:45.478 --> 00:01:48.200
He told us to be patient and that everything would work out."

25
00:01:52.304 --> 00:01:53.345
Miles sighed again.

26
00:01:53.365 --> 00:01:59.667
"Unfortunately, my father wouldn't allow the engagement to be broken.

27
00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:03.869
He felt it would reflect badly upon our family."

28
00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:08.291
"So did Edith marry Arthur?"

29
00:02:08.311 --> 00:02:13.554
"No, my brother Hugh declared that he was in love with Edith.

30
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:18.556
But everyone knew he was really in love with her money.

31
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.945
The only person he fooled was my father, who always treats Hugh like his favorite son."

32
00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.910
Edward remembered how Miles had protected him.

33
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:35.073
"I can't believe you let Hugh get away with that."

34
00:02:35.093 --> 00:02:41.980
"I was a wild young man, but I wasn't a bad person," Miles said.

35
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.084
"However, Hugh exaggerated my faults to our father.

36
00:02:47.852 --> 00:02:50.954
He bribed a servant to help him hide a rope ladder in my room.

37
00:02:52.275 --> 00:02:56.077
Then Hugh told our father that I was planning to elope with Edith."

38
00:02:56.097 --> 00:02:58.218
"But Hugh was lying!"

39
00:02:59.899 --> 00:03:01.620
Edward pounded his fist on the table.

40
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.502
"Exactly," Miles said.

41
00:03:04.522 --> 00:03:08.104
"My father was furious with me.

42
00:03:09.685 --> 00:03:14.208
He made me join the army, thinking three years as a soldier would teach me a lesson.

43
00:03:16.072 --> 00:03:20.734
In my last battle, I was captured by the enemy and spent seven years in prison.

44
00:03:23.376 --> 00:03:27.598
I recently escaped and am on my way home after ten years."

45
00:03:27.618 --> 00:03:30.539
"That's outrageous!"

46
00:03:31.479 --> 00:03:33.180
Edward jumped up from the table.

47
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:37.462
"As your king, I will make things right.

48
00:03:38.683 --> 00:03:40.824
Now let me tell you my story."

49
00:03:43.632 --> 00:03:46.633
Edward launched into his tale of switching clothes with Tom.

50
00:03:48.975 --> 00:03:50.515
Miles listened in amazement.

51
00:03:50.535 --> 00:03:57.538
"For a pauper, Edward knows a lot about the royal family and the palace," he thought.

52
00:03:57.558 --> 00:04:00.080
"Poor child.

53
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.742
I'll make sure he gets the care he needs until he's well again.

54
00:04:06.102 --> 00:04:09.304
And until then, I'll just go along with whatever he says."

55
00:04:11.176 --> 00:04:13.938
Edward finished his story at the point where he met Miles.

56
00:04:13.958 --> 00:04:22.442
"You saved me from shame and injury, and possibly saved my life and my crown," Edward said.

57
00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.643
"How can I reward you?"

58
00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:30.046
"I just did what any loyal subject would do," Miles said.

59
00:04:30.066 --> 00:04:32.908
"I don't need anything in return."

60
00:04:34.969 --> 00:04:36.910
But Edward insisted on rewarding him.

61
00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:42.261
"Well, there is one thing," Miles said.

62
00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:47.564
"Back in history, there was a man who was not required to remove his hat whenever he was

63
00:04:47.624 --> 00:04:48.184
with the king.

64
00:04:49.245 --> 00:04:53.848
I'd like to have a similar privilege—I'd like to be allowed to sit when you sit."

65
00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:58.831
"A reasonable request," Edward said.

66
00:04:58.851 --> 00:05:04.254
"And one that I grant not only to you, but to your heirs.

67
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:07.116
In addition I will make you a knight."

68
00:05:08.996 --> 00:05:11.799
Miles handed Edward his sword and knelt before him.

69
00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.482
Edward tapped him on each shoulder with the sword.

70
00:05:15.502 --> 00:05:18.564
"Rise, Sir Miles!

71
00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.325
And sit down!"

72
00:05:20.345 --> 00:05:27.611
"Thank goodness," Miles thought, "Edward is now permitting me to sit.

73
00:05:29.073 --> 00:05:32.936
Otherwise, I'd be standing until he was cured of this delusion that he's king!"

74
00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.302
By this point both Edward and Miles were exhausted.

75
00:05:41.104 --> 00:05:43.686
Edward stood up and went over to Miles' bed.

76
00:05:45.988 --> 00:05:48.371
He seemed to assume that it was his place to sleep.

77
00:05:49.712 --> 00:05:52.134
Miles had assumed that Edward would sleep on the floor.

78
00:05:52.154 --> 00:05:56.017
"It's time for you to help me get ready for bed."

79
00:05:57.799 --> 00:05:58.860
Edward sat on the bed.

80
00:06:01.282 --> 00:06:03.024
Miles helped Edward remove his shoes.

81
00:06:06.688 --> 00:06:09.469
"And where am I to sleep?"

82
00:06:09.489 --> 00:06:11.770
"You will lie in front of the door and guard it."

83
00:06:15.991 --> 00:06:18.352
Edward lay down and promptly fell asleep.

84
00:06:19.892 --> 00:06:22.453
Miles watched the sleeping child and smiled.

85
00:06:22.473 --> 00:06:28.415
"He could have been born into the royal family—he plays the part so naturally.

86
00:06:29.715 --> 00:06:31.136
Sleep well, my little king."

87
00:06:35.804 --> 00:06:40.273
Then Miles stretched out on the floor in front of the door and went to sleep too.
